                <pb facs="0437" n="407" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v15/pg407"/>

                <head>167. Memorandum From the President’s Special Assistant (Rostow) to President Johnson<anchor n="1" xml:id="d167-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1966-09-16T17:15:00-04:00">September 16, 1966, 5:15 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. President:</p>
                <p>This is a probably reliable report of an Erhard backgrounder.</p>
                <p>From all evidence, Erhard is a man with a
                    dilemma and no plan to get out of it.</p>
                <pb facs="0438" n="408" xml:id="pg408"/>
                <p>We must lead him out.</p>
                <p>We are working hard—State, Treasury, Francis—to have a plan ready.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Walt</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d167-a1.xml" xpointer="d167-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
